  "query_preview": "..\n(Tuesday through next Sunday)\nIssued at 1021 PM CDT Sat Sep 5 2026\n\nUnfortunately, the main story continues to be the heat. By Tuesday, \nthe high pressure shifts back over the southeastern US, and \ntemperatures will warm in response. Highs will be back in the mid-\n90s Wednesday. It won't be quite as hot and humid as what we've \nbeen experiencing lately, but it'll still be uncomfortable with \ntemperatures that are well above normal for September. A pattern \nchange on Thursday brings a front into the area which increases \nrain chances into the weekend. While this front drops temperatures\nsome, it won't be as strong as you may hope for as above normal \ntemperatures continue to be favored.",
